**Read:** [Management of Protective Relay Settings — FIST 6-4](../sources/Management-of-Protective-Relay-Settings-FIST.lingua#r_11X2AGDKXQ69S5GZYNK21Y8CW6), entire change/evidence and communication work examples; [MATPOWER User’s Manual, version 8.1](../sources/MATPOWER-User-Manual-8-1.lingua#r_5ANPNGQHP93EVQXR6FW357WSEV), complete model/version and case/solver notice context; [Hybrid Symbolic-Numeric Framework — Cui, Li and Tomsovic](../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK), entire reproducible model/method comparison.

A power-system model is a maintained technical claim tied to actual equipment, topology, state, material, settings and measurements. Record units, bases, sign conventions, versions, uncertainty and the source of each consequential parameter. A file named final does not establish that it still represents the installed system after a change.

Trace one decision from physical requirements through books/methods, model, independent calculation, test and service evidence. Identify what must be rechecked after changing a transformer, source, control, protection setting, solver version or operating duty. Preserve the disagreement and revision when an observation contradicts the earlier account.

Keep original explanations and independent teaching examples here, with complete authorized external sources. A free-readable book, open-licensed text, proprietary guide, standard, open-source solver and case dataset have distinct rights and evidence. Share generic quantitative, field, metrology and computational knowledge through their existing Records; keep power-specific reasoning where it explains the actual system. This supports continuous learning and maintenance without requiring every reader to traverse every connected field before asking a useful electrical question.

**Continue:** [A full practical and graduate power-engineering programme](../study/A-full-practical-and-graduate-power-engineering-programme.lingua#r_762ATXJ9563BT8M3229MP1G1FR).

